"""
Given an integer, determine if that number is a prime number or a negative prime number.

- A prime number is a positive integer greater than 1 that is only divisible by 1 and itself.
- A negative prime number is the negative version of a positive prime number.
- 1 and 0 are not considered prime numbers.
"""

# CODE #

is_unnatural_prime = lambda n: True if len(list(filter(lambda x:abs(n)//x==abs(n)/x, [i for i in range(abs(n)+1)][1:])))==2 else False # If the length of the list of multiples of the absolute value of n is 2, return True, otherwise False
